    {
      "id": "commentary",
      "html": "<h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The text (on imported marble) would have been fixed to the base of a statue of the Genius of the city of Catania, probably erected on the stage-building of the theatre. The Genius was the protective spirit of a person or a thing. Dedications to the Genius of the Emperor were common, but also to cities (e.g. both a statue and temple of the Genius of the city of Lilybaeum = Marsala are mentioned in other inscriptions). Facundus Porfyrius is not otherwise known. The precise significance of 'cons eiusdem' in line 7 is extensively debated and several alternatives have been suggested: the most likely interpretation is 'consularis eiusdem', signifying consularis of the same city, i.e. Catania, and so by extension / implication the province of Sicily.</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "bibliography",
      "html": "<h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> 1959.0022 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283</a>  </li><li> 3778 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000352\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000352</a>  </li><li> Mommsen 1883 <a href=\"http://arachne.uni-koeln.de/item/buchseite/650756\" target=\"_blank\">7014</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589</a>  </li><li> Holm 1925 43-44 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001919\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001919</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1958-1959 5-10 fig.1 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001856\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001856</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1988 69 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427</a>  </li><li> Wilson 1990 187 fig.156.b <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1993 560, 583 fig.19 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001827\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001827</a>  </li><li> Korhonen 2004 7 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "handnote",
      "html": " <p>The letters are deeply but somewhat irregularly cut, with some internal variation (e.g. A appears with both broken and straight bar; E appears both as a tall narrow standard E and as a vertical stroke with a single horizontal bar across the middle; V appears both as V and as Y). Interpuncts are mostly absent, except after VC and CONS in the final two lines.</p> Line 1  60-80  Line 2-4  40-60  Line 5-7  50-70      "
    },
